        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_1971668492": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-1f15d09fdf@example.invalid",
          "leftPadding": "3",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-b3eaac8b1c@example.invalid",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Feb 06 2025 18:52:38 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><b><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">The</span></span></b></span><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><b>&nbsp;standard&nbsp;</b></span></span><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><b><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">in HA cement.</span></span></b></span></span></p>\n<p>HydroSet is a self-setting, calcium phosphate cement intended for use in the repair of neurosurgical burr holes, contiguous craniotomy cuts and other cranial defects as well as in the augmentation or restoration of bony contour in the craniofacial skeleton.<br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Feb 19 2025 22:08:22 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "5",
          "textIsRich": "true"
